# --- Answer keys and generators: defence in depth -------------------------------
# These live OUTSIDE this repository by design (D11.1, A8) — placement is the
# primary control. The patterns below are insurance against an accidental copy
# landing inside the tree, NOT enforcement: `git add -f` still overrides them,
# and a key committed to public history is permanent.
#
# The pattern MUST name the held-out key exactly and MUST NOT be a case variant of
# the public dev key's name. `core.ignorecase` is true on Windows, so an earlier
# `ANSWER_KEY*` rule silently matched `datasets/*/answer_key.json` and excluded all
# three PUBLIC dev keys from the repository — the dev split shipped with no keys at
# all, and a fresh clone could not run a single dev-split test (D38).
holdout_answer_key.json
holdout_invoice_index.json
README.original.md
answer-keys/
**/answer-keys/
_generators/
**/_generators/

# --- Run ledger (D9) ------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived, local-only, and regenerable from the scorecard directory, so losing it
# costs nothing. `[P2]` fixed the filename as `run-ledger.jsonl` (D75); the bare name
# with no slash matches at any depth, so the ledger is ignored wherever the scorecard
# directory is put.
run-ledger.jsonl
*.ledger.jsonl

# NOTE: scorecards are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the durable,
# tamper-evident record (D9) and are meant to be committed. Do not add them here.

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
# Written by `pip install .`, which D59 made a documented step (the console scripts only
# exist once installed). Both land beside the sources rather than in a temp directory.
build/
dist/

# --- Scratch files the runbook tells a reader to create ---------------------------
# docs/RUNBOOK.md §2.6 has the reader write a throwaway findings artifact in the repo
# root to try scoring. Anchored to the root and named exactly, so a real fixture living
# deeper in the tree is unaffected: an ignore rule that quietly excluded something the
# repository must ship is the defect D42 and D44 were both about.
/empty.json
/findings.json

# --- Session / tooling artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# Written per project by the Claude Code session tooling: a timestamp and a
# `claude --resume <id>` command. Machine- and session-specific, so it is useless to
# anyone else and would churn on every run.
resume_session.txt

# --- OS / editor junk -----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
